                                                                                   )
                                                                     ]
                                                  ]
                              ] ;
              fma:definition "A graft is a segment of healthy tissue transplanted from one area of a person's body to another. Unlike a flap, a graft initially relies solely on diffusion for nourishment, and its blood supply is later established through neovascularization—primarily via newly formed capillary networks—which develops a significant time after transplantation." ;
              rdfs:label "Surgical graft"@en .


