            obo:IAO_0000115 "Flap surgery involves transporting healthy, live tissue from one location of the body to another - often to areas that have lost skin, fat, muscle movement, and/or skeletal support. There are several different types of flaps that may be utilized, depending upon the location of the flap and the structures that need to be repaired." ;
            obo:IAO_0000119 """https://stanfordhealthcare.org/medical-treatments/p/plastic-surgery/procedures/flap.html 
retrieved 27.5.2025, 19:56""" ;
            rdfs:label "Surgical flap"@en .


